bevy_render 0.19.0: let the app pass the platform display to the wgpu instance

wgpu's GLES backend creates its EGL display at *instance* creation.  bevy_render
creates the instance with `display: None`, so on GLES the EGL display is the
surfaceless platform, and presenting to a Wayland window then fails
("Initialized platform Unknown doesn't work with window Wayland" / incompatible
window kind).  That leaves Bevy with no working backend on a machine that has
Mesa GL but no Vulkan driver -- anonymOS in a VM (llvmpipe).

Add a `RenderDisplayHandle` resource: when one is present before RenderPlugin
builds (the app copies bevy_winit's DisplayHandleWrapper into it), the instance
is created against that display.  Vulkan/Metal/DX12 ignore the field.

Also, on the GL backend, cap max_storage_textures_per_shader_stage at 4 so the
SSAO plugin stays off: naga's GLSL output for SSAO's depth prepass calls
textureGatherOffset(sampler2DShadow, vec2, ivec2, int), which no GLSL version
accepts, so creating that pipeline at startup brings the whole renderer down.

Applied by scripts/build-ratty.sh to the checksum-verified bevy_render-0.19.0
.crate unpacked in deps/ratty/anonymos-crates/.
